// What Kimi (moonshotai/kimi-k2.5) wrote for the SAME resolution logic
// when given only a natural-language task description (mirroring the
// real historical respondsTo bug's framing) and NO Thermite contract --
// see dev-journal for the exact prompt and full transcript. Kimi's
// actual output was `match (commit_in_own_log, foreign_repo_accepted) {
// (true, true) => true, _ => false }`; Thermite doesn't parse tuple-
// pattern match, so this is the semantically identical `&&` form --
// preserves the exact bug (gates resolution on foreign_repo_accepted),
// which is the only thing this probe is checking.
//
// Reproduces the real historical bug's shape almost exactly: gates
// resolution on foreign_repo_accepted, an illegal repo-local-determinism
// violation (SPEC.md SS18, issue #69). Checked here against the SAME
// contract ../repo_local_determinism.th already certifies against (which
// Kimi, given the contract directly instead, satisfied correctly -- see
// the other dispatch in the same session).
// Expected: `forge check` FAILS with "postcondition not satisfied".

fn resolves(commit_in_own_log: bool, foreign_repo_accepted: bool) -> bool
  req true
  ens result == commit_in_own_log
  fx  pure
{
  commit_in_own_log && foreign_repo_accepted
}
